# Client names that stay text, reviewed one by one (scan_client_names reads this file).
# One line each: file | name | why it stays text. A line matches that name in that file's quoted
# text only (comments are never shown in the game and are grouped apart); the scan lists lines
# that no longer match anything, to be removed.

# --- our own words that equal a client name
crates/esurv/src/main.rs | Setup | our file's name, "Eternal Survivors Setup.exe" (an English word, not the spell)
crates/esurv-setup/Cargo.toml | Setup | the crate's description names our file, "Eternal Survivors Setup.exe"; never shown in the game
crates/esurv-setup/src/lib.rs | Setup | our file's name, "Eternal Survivors Setup.exe", which the updater reads out of the release zip (an English word, not the spell)
crates/esurv-app/src/update/unzip.rs | Setup | test fixture: our setup's file name in a test zip (an English word, not the spell)
crates/esurv-server/src/game/pickups.rs | Restoration | our pickup's name, the Restoration Rune (an English word, not the talent tree)
crates/esurv-sim/src/game/lines.rs | Restoration | the Restoration Rune pickup's line, our pickup's name (an English word, not the talent tree)
content/classes.ron | Claw | "the Claw": the Claw Tentacle, our pet (a creature, like the enemies), not the spell
crates/esurv-server/src/ground.rs | Human | a client file path (World\Generic\Human\...) the test reads a model from, not a race's name

